title: "[pallet-broker] Prevent auto-renewal from renewing another task's workload"
doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    `enable_auto_renew` previously renewed whatever renewable workload was found on the given
    core index without checking that it belongs to the given task. Since a core index can be
    assigned a different workload each bulk period, a task could end up paying to renew a
    completely unrelated task's workload, and the stored auto-renewal record would keep charging
    it every sale.

    `enable_auto_renew` now only renews immediately if the expiring workload includes the task.
    Otherwise it requires a `workload_end_hint` pointing at a renewal record that includes the
    task, and fails with the new `TaskNotInWorkload` error if it does not. Automatic
    renewal processing re-checks this before charging the task's sovereign account and emits
    `AutoRenewalFailed` (dropping the record) on a mismatch. Additionally, when enabling triggers
    an immediate renewal, `next_renewal` is now set to the end of the renewed period instead of
    the `workload_end_hint`, which previously caused the next renewal to be skipped.
crates:
- name: pallet-broker
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: coretime-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
